{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**Yes.** As of 6 November 2026, CBI UCITS Q&A 1088 permits listed ETF and unlisted share classes within the same UCITS/sub-fund. The prospectus must clearly compare relevant differences in:\n\n- **Dealing:** subscription/redemption routes, primary versus secondary markets, frequency, cut-offs and cash/in-kind arrangements.\n- **Settlement:** procedures and settlement periods.\n- **Costs:** fees, expenses and dealing costs—including exchange brokerage and bid–offer spreads—and their allocation.\n- **Minimums:** applicable minimum subscriptions, holdings and redemptions.\n- **Rights:** any differences in shareholder rights, including voting and distributions.\n- **Liquidity:** access to fund redemptions versus exchange trading, and associated liquidity limitations.\n- **Price:** NAV-based dealing for unlisted classes versus exchange prices for ETF shares, including possible premiums or discounts to NAV.\n\n**Worth knowing:** This is the Irish disclosure framework, not a requirement to satisfy US ETF share-class exemptive conditions."}}
